 "issues": [
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "REPORT Method states the pi0 coupling as (N_c e^2/48 pi^2 f) eps^{mu nu a b} d_mu A_nu A_a d_b pi0; with d_mu A_nu this is a factor 2 too small and inconsistent with the quoted amplitude N_c e^2/(12 pi^2 f). The code (symbolic_derivations.py) correctly uses (d_mu A_nu - d_nu A_mu) = F_mu nu. Cross-check derivation from B-H eq. 67: N_c e^2/(48 pi^2 f) eps F A d pi0 = N_c e^2/(24 pi^2 f) eps dA A d pi0. Numbers unaffected.",
   "suggested_fix": "Replace d_mu A_nu by F_mu nu in the text (or use 24 pi^2)."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "Convergence claim \"X = 25, 50, 100, 200, 400 ... agree to within 5e-8 relative in Lambda\" is not what hedgehog_log.txt shows: X = 25 differs by 8e-7 in Lambda, 1.2e-6 in C and B = 0.99999944. The 5e-8 spread holds for X = 100-400.",
   "suggested_fix": "Say \"X = 100-400 agree to 5e-8; X = 25 is off by ~1e-6\"."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "Summary/REPORT: \"the neutron enclosed charge peaks at +0.185 at 1 fm\" is a sampling artifact of the table grid. Its true maximum is +0.206 at R = 0.73 fm (massless ANW); massive AN84: +0.140 at 0.68 fm.",
   "suggested_fix": "Quote the peak (+0.206 at 0.73 fm) or say \"reaches +0.185 at 1 fm\"."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "\"38/38 symbolic checks pass\" includes check 10d, hard-coded True \"by inspection\" (not computed), and checks 5c/7b that pass only up to an overall sign. The statements are true (the cross-check confirms them), but 38/38 overstates what was computed.",
   "suggested_fix": "Mark 10d as an inspection, not a computed check (37 computed + 1 by inspection)."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "Verdict vocabulary: CALIBRATED is used for internal checks with no literature target (symbolic derivations, integral charges); QUANTIFIED is used for a SEED 6B claim although PLAN reserves it for \u00a78 gaps. The 6B paraphrase \"one parameter set covers all predictions (anomaly sector included)\" is the agent's, not SEED.md's wording.",
   "suggested_fix": "Use \"check passed\" for internal checks; label the f_pi tension as a confirmed preregistered prediction (no SEED verdict) or AMENDED."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "SEED 6B AMENDED: the headline \"3 of 7 within 30%\" counts mu_p (-33%), mu_n (-31%), g_piNN (-32%) as failures of \"roughly 30%\". The amendment is really carried by g_A (-52%) and the infinite r_p, <r^2>_n in the massless model. The verdict holds; the framing overstates it.",
   "suggested_fix": "State that 6 of 7 finite quantities are within ~33%; the exceptions are g_A and the individual charge radii."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "Commitment 4 CONFIRMED: the preregistered test passes (the isovector radius diverges linearly; finite with m_pi). But any extended charge distribution has an R-dependent enclosed charge, so the test does not tell \"dressing\" from ordinary structure, and \"not slowed\" holds by construction. The caveat is in the report; the verdict word is generous.",
   "suggested_fix": "Write \"CONFIRMED in the preregistered operational sense (classical pion-cloud structure, not vacuum polarization)\"."
  },
